# Faithless Looting cast for {R} (Mox Ruby) goes to the graveyard. On turn 3 it is flashed back for {2}{R} (Mox Ruby, Mox Jet
# and a Mountain): "then exile it" (CR 702.34a), so it ends in exile and a second flashback is refused (nothing in the
# graveyard to cast). The refusal's positive control is the flashback just taken.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Faithless Looting
Mountain
Mountain
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Island; Island)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Graveyard.Faithless Looting.Cast(Ability: Flashback)
! Bot1.Graveyard.Faithless Looting.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Faithless Looting
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Mox Jet; Mountain
